/* SPDX-License-Identifier: proprietary */
/*
 * 0x021  ACU_discharge_interlock -- RX from the AMS. The two facts only the AMS
 * can observe, published so the ECU can decide whether to secure the DC-link
 * discharge (#198).
 *
 * >>> MIRRORS isc-fs/IFS08-CE-AMS Core/Inc/can/messages/acu_discharge_interlock.def
 * >>> FIELD FOR FIELD. The AMS owns this layout. Diff the two on any AMS bump.
 *
 * NOT A REQUEST. Both fields are raw observations. The AMS deliberately does not
 * send a pre-computed "please discharge", because the ECU owns the third term --
 * its own DC-link measurement -- and routing that decision through a CAN frame
 * would put a stale value in the middle of the judgement. The ECU therefore
 * computes:
 *
 *     secure = fsm_in_start AND tsms AND (own dc_bus > DischargeReleaseV)
 *
 * latched on entry, released on the ECU's own measurement falling. See
 * discharge.hpp.
 *
 * The first cut of this file got it wrong: it declared a single `request` bit at
 * bit 0 and ignored bit 1. Bit 0 is fsm_in_start, so the ECU read "the AMS is in
 * Start" as a complete instruction to discharge -- tsms never entered the
 * decision, and with a drained link and a stale 0x466 it would secure on every
 * entry to Start and hold to the 30 s timeout. Kept in the history deliberately:
 * two repos agreeing on an ID while disagreeing about its fields is the failure
 * mode this comment exists to prevent.
 */

CAN_MSG(ACU_discharge_interlock, 0x021, 1, "AMS", 100)
    /* FSM is in Start: AIR-, AIR+ and precharge are ALL commanded open, so any
     * voltage on the link is left over rather than something the AMS is putting
     * there. Excludes Precharge/Transition, where the link is deliberately
     * rising through the resistor and a forced discharge would fight it. */
    FIELD_LE_BITS (fsm_in_start, uint8_t, 0, 1, 1, 0, "bool")
    /* Shutdown circuit is complete (AMS PF9). Any open shutdown element pulls
     * this low, so tsms = 1 means the discharge relay is energised and the bleed
     * is DISCONNECTED -- the normal discharge path is NOT running, which is
     * exactly the condition under which a stranded link needs the ECU. */
    FIELD_LE_BITS (tsms,         uint8_t, 1, 1, 1, 0, "bool")
CAN_MSG_END(ACU_discharge_interlock)
